  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Circular Textile Capacity and Trade Platform</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh&#x2019;s Ready-Made Garment (RMG) sector stands at a strategic crossroad. With the country set to graduate from Least Developed Country (LDC) status in 2026, the sector must shift from cost-based production to value-based, future-proofed models that align with global sustainability standards. At the same time, new European Union (EU) regulations such as the Ecodesign for Sustainable Products Regulation (ESPR), Corporate Sustainability Reporting Directive (CSRD), and Digital Product Passport (DPP) demand that suppliers not only comply with circularity standards but also understand and communicate them effectively. To reach this transformation cross-border cooperation is very much needed. This project will support this cooperation by establishing a Circular Trade &amp; Training Platform, designed to equip the next generation of Bangladeshi apparel leaders with the practical tools, knowledge, and networks to lead in the global circular economy. The Platform aims to support Bangladesh&#x2019;s tier 1, 2 and 3 textile companies in joining the global circular textile transition by empowering them to become circular. This will be done through the creation of a leadership training and trading platform that connects Dutch and Bangladeshi textile stakeholders through content, dialogue, and trade.</narrative>
  </description>
